{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for \\(a_{100}\\) in the sequence defined by \\(a_0 = 2\\), \\(a_1 = 1\\), and \\(a_n = a_{n-1} \\sqrt{3} - a_{n-2}\\) for \\(n \\geq 2\\), we start by examining the first few terms of the sequence to identify any patterns.\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(a_2\\):\n\\[\na_2 = a_1 \\sqrt{3} - a_0 = 1 \\cdot \\sqrt{3} - 2 = \\sqrt{3} - 2.\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(a_3\\):\n\\[\na_3 = a_2 \\sqrt{3} - a_1 = (\\sqrt{3} - 2) \\sqrt{3} - 1 = 3 - 2\\sqrt{3} - 1 = 2 - 2\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(a_4\\):\n\\[\na_4 = a_3 \\sqrt{3} - a_2 = (2 - 2\\sqrt{3}) \\sqrt{3} - (\\sqrt{3} - 2) = 2\\sqrt{3} - 6 - \\sqrt{3} + 2 = \\sqrt{3} - 4.\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(a_5\\):\n\\[\na_5 = a_4 \\sqrt{3} - a_3 = (\\sqrt{3} - 4) \\sqrt{3} - (2 - 2\\sqrt{3}) = 3 - 4\\sqrt{3} - 2 + 2\\sqrt{3} = 1 - 2\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(a_6\\):\n\\[\na_6 = a_5 \\sqrt{3} - a_4 = (1 - 2\\sqrt{3}) \\sqrt{3} - (\\sqrt{3} - 4) = \\sqrt{3} - 6 - \\sqrt{3} + 4 = -2.\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(a_7\\):\n\\[\na_7 = a_6 \\sqrt{3} - a_5 = (-2) \\sqrt{3} - (1 - 2\\sqrt{3}) = -2\\sqrt{3} - 1 + 2\\sqrt{3} = -1.\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(a_8\\):\n\\[\na_8 = a_7 \\sqrt{3} - a_6 = (-1) \\sqrt{3} - (-2) = -\\sqrt{3} + 2.\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":1122,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,17767,64,15159,16,15,15,11035,8,304,279,8500,4512,553,17767,64,62,15,284,220,17,59,701,17767,64,62,16,284,220,16,59,701,323,17767,64,1089,284,264,15159,77,12,16,92,1124,26888,90,18,92,481,264,15159,77,12,17,11035,8,369,17767,77,1124,709,80,220,17,59,701,582,1191,553,37836,279,1156,2421,3793,315,279,8500,311,10542,894,12624,382,5338,11,582,11047,17767,64,62,17,59,982,59,9640,64,62,17,284,264,62,16,1124,26888,90,18,92,481,264,62,15,284,220,16,1124,50853,1124,26888,90,18,92,481,220,17,284,1124,26888,90,18,92,481,220,17,624,59,2533,584